  "goodToKnow": "Der Grenzübergang is a border crossing. During the division of Germany, crossings like Checkpoint Charlie and Helmstedt-Marienborn were heavily guarded. On the night of 9 November 1989, the Bornholmer Straße crossing in Berlin was the first to open under the pressure of crowds. Within the Schengen Area there are normally no checks, although Germany reintroduced temporary checks at its land borders in 2024. Plural: die Grenzübergänge."
